Triangles $BPC$ and $\triangle ACD$ are congruent on the angles $\angle BPC$ and $\angle ACD,$ so their respective non-aligned legs are proportional. Let $x$ be the length of the edge connecting vertex $B$ to the base along the same line as $PC.$ Then

\boxed{ \ \ds x = \sin 60^\circ \times h/2 }

The pyramid has 5 edges, each of length $x$ except for the height, which is $h.$ Thus, the sum of the lengths of the edges of the pyramid is

\boxed{ 5x + h }

Now, we determine $h.$

By the Pythagorean theorem in $\triangle APB,$

